diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index b024ca1..3a3b4ce 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -27145,7 +27145,19 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: help of the setting of HDR at more than 8 bits where the graphics send RGB at 8 bits at most; translated in Estuary (#32511)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#41012"
-msgid "For older NVIDIA cards (GeForce GTX 10 and GTX 16, RTX 20, TITAN V) that send RGB at only 8 bits over HDMI. On: HDR goes out in a format that carries 10 or 12 bits (YCbCr 4:2:2) where the TV and the picture mode allow it, which reduces banding. Where they do not, HDR goes out as before. Dolby Vision and SDR are not affected. Off until this is confirmed on those cards. Takes effect from the next video."
+msgid "For NVIDIA cards whose HDMI output would send HDR in RGB at only 8 bits: GeForce GTX 10, GTX 16 and RTX 20, TITAN V, and other cards at 4K 50 or 60 Hz without an HDMI 2.1 link. On: HDR goes out as YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits instead (10 on GeForce GTX 10 and TITAN V), at the same link speed, which reduces banding and keeps all the colour detail of the video. Dolby Vision and SDR are not affected. Takes effect from the next video."
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: label of the setting of RGB at 12 bits first for HDR on GeForce GTX 16 and RTX 20 (NVIDIA); translated in Estuary (#32512)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41013"
+msgid "RGB at 12 bits first (GeForce GTX 16, RTX 20)"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of the setting of RGB at 12 bits first for HDR on GeForce GTX 16 and RTX 20 (NVIDIA); translated in Estuary (#32513)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41014"
+msgid "Only for GeForce GTX 16 and RTX 20 cards, which have no 10 bits in RGB over HDMI. On: where the TV takes 36-bit deep colour and the mode fits (up to 4K at 30 Hz on HDMI 2.0), HDR goes out in RGB at 12 bits rather than YCbCr 4:2:2, which keeps the full colour detail of menus and subtitles but runs the link 1.5 times faster. Some TVs show nothing with it: if yours does, stop the video and turn this off."
 msgstr ""
 
 
